{"agent":"recover-4f","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`deadline_s` is applied as a fresh per-call `timeout` on worktree add, rev-parse, merge-base, and merge, not as one budget for the whole scratch merge. Given `probe_timeout_s=5`, a slow `worktree add` can run 5s and then `merge` another 5s (and merge-base yet another 5s if it is killed: non-zero `.code` is treated as \"not an ancestor\" and the merge is still attempted). `probe._scratch` now blocks in-process on `CI.merge_tree` with no outer cap, so the CLI stays alive well past `[locks].probe_timeout_s` — the outliving-the-deadline failure this change claims to close.","digest":"5887eddd040d459b","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/ci/scratch.py:141","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/ci/scratch.py:141"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"`left()` is `cutoff - time.monotonic()` with no floor, while `W.scratch_tree` is still given the original `deadline_s` as its own timer, which starts after `cutoff`. A worktree add that finishes inside that timer but after the shared cutoff makes `left()` negative, and the next call is `W.git(..., timeout=left())`. `subprocess` rejects a negative timeout with `ValueError` instead of a cannot-merge/`timed_out` result. Given `deadline_s=5`, add starts ~50ms after `cutoff` with `timeout=5` and returns at cutoff+10ms: `rev-parse`/`merge-base` is invoked with `timeout≈-0.01` and the probe raises rather than reporting unavailable.","digest":"d4bef26204969ecf","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/ci/scratch.py:left","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/ci/scratch.py:left"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_findings":1,"delta_from":"6342919fae17f7994e6933c774d85eff58d1791c","delta_raised":["d4bef26204969ecf"],"delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":3875,"diff_sha":"920cad9e41d41188d7fc1faf83ec7eb49a2380b15e7e8fde8cd9cdf7133f8368","diff_source":"delta review of 2 commits since 6342919fae","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":96.3,"family":"xai","findings":2,"full_coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"1aca6eea503d8e2c","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/LK-probe-scratch-deadline.critic.grok-4.7.20261108T152549Z-ba81fc0d.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"delta","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"7a19aaba37e8f83ee0e3e76318ef5a85a101517d","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/infra/worktree/_locate.py":"100644 7fc42073c28481bf58fab03272504a2b9009c05f","ddflow/services/ci/scratch.py":"100644 3f5ac148ed22801d6ed3f4909f0afe5c05813ec0","ddflow/services/probe.py":"100644 10401239be1b3f8b901c8f173d7c177b27da89b1","tests/test_conflict_probe.py":"100644 ed84294e3d7bbdf0b0b548edd72cd0aaef69c205"},"reviewer":"grok-4.7","reviewer_digest":"1857ec352c55ee94","reviewer_families":["google","xai"],"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","superseded":["5887eddd040d459b"],"titles":["ddflow/services/ci/scratch.py:141","ddflow/services/ci/scratch.py:left"],"tree_sha":"7a19aaba37e8+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"critic","reason":"1 finding(s)"},"id":"eb17396c97e76a2a0f03bdf8a","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":155611,"schema":1,"subject":"LK-probe-scratch-deadline","ts":"2026-11-08T15:27:26.250403Z"}
{"agent":"recover-4f","data":{"digest":"d4bef26204969ecf","finding":2,"gate":"critic","location":"ddflow/services/ci/scratch.py:left","probe":"The premise (probe RAISES) is false: subprocess.run raises TimeoutExpired for a negative timeout, not ValueError (verified: subprocess.run(['true'], timeout=-0.01) -> TimeoutExpired; timeout=0.0 -> TimeoutExpired), and G.run catches TimeoutExpired and returns GitResult(unavailable, timed_out=True), which merge_tree reports as a cannot-merge failure -> the probe is UNAVAILABLE, never a crash. I also floored left() at 0 (max(0.0, ...)) so an exhausted budget is an explicit immediate clean timeout.","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/ci/scratch.py:left","verdict":"refuted"},"id":"e3cb4aaa3253b27a13ad37e0f","kind":"review.triaged","lamport":155622,"schema":1,"subject":"LK-probe-scratch-deadline","ts":"2026-11-08T15:28:34.501126Z"}
